{#
  PROJECT CARD — one row of the My Work section (Figma 184:13749).

  A ROW, NOT A CARD, despite the name: screenshot on the left, details on the
  right, the two separated by a rule from the row above. The name is kept
  because it is the projects.js entry it renders, and because a v2 component of
  the same name occupied this slot before the cleanup sweep — that one was a
  fixed-width carousel slide and shares no markup with this.

  THE NUMBER IS PRESENTATIONAL. It is the position in the section, not a
  property of the project, so it is passed in rather than stored in projects.js
  — reordering the array renumbers the cards with no data edit. It is
  aria-hidden for the same reason: "01" read aloud before the title adds
  nothing a sighted user gets from it.

  The whole row is NOT one link. Only the pill is, because the screenshot has
  no accessible name and wrapping both in a single anchor would put the image
  inside the link's text alternative for no benefit.

  THE MEDIA SLOT IS EITHER A LOOP OR A STILL, decided by whether projects.js
  found encodes on disk. Both branches carry .work-card__image so _work.css
  sizes them with one rule and the box keeps its own aspect-ratio either way.

  NO `autoplay` ATTRIBUTE ON THE VIDEO, deliberately. scripts/work-motion.js
  owns playback so it can check prefers-reduced-motion BEFORE anything moves or
  is fetched; `autoplay` would start the loop the moment the file was parsed and
  a reduced-motion visitor would catch a frame of movement before JS could pause
  it. The cost is that a no-JS visitor gets the poster and no loop, which is the
  right way round for a decorative thumbnail.

  READ MORE IS CONDITIONAL, and stays that way even though all three rows
  currently have a `url`. button.njk silently degrades a missing href to
  <button type=button> — a control that looks live and does nothing — so the
  guard is what stops a future carded-but-unlinked project from shipping one.
  A url pointing at an unbuilt page is a different case and renders normally.

  PROPS
    project  a projects.js entry — needs .card {title, body}, .title; .url and
             .motion may both be null
    index    1-based position; rendered as 01/02/03 and used for the alt text
#}

{% from "components/button.njk" import button %}

{% macro projectCard(project, index) %}
  <article class="work-card">
    <div class="work-card__media">
      {#
        The exported fill is 692 wide against a 594 box, so `cover` crops 49px
        from each side — which is exactly what the comp does. Do not export the
        594-wide frame instead: that bakes the crop in and the art no longer
        reflows if the column ratio ever changes. The loops follow the same
        rule at their own native widths.
      #}
      {%- set poster = "/Assets/images/work/" + project.slug + "-card.png" %}
      {%- if project.motion %}
        <video
          class="work-card__image"
          data-work-motion
          poster="{{ poster }}"
          width="{{ project.motion.w }}"
          height="{{ project.motion.h }}"
          role="img"
          aria-label="{{ project.title }} — interface screens"
          loop
          muted
          playsinline
          preload="none"
          disablepictureinpicture
          draggable="false"
        >
          {%- if project.motion.webm %}<source src="{{ project.motion.webm }}" type="video/webm" />{% endif %}
          {%- if project.motion.mp4 %}<source src="{{ project.motion.mp4 }}" type="video/mp4" />{% endif %}
        </video>
      {%- else %}
        <img
          class="work-card__image"
          src="{{ poster }}"
          alt="{{ project.title }} — interface screens"
          width="{{ 692 }}"
          height="{{ 476 }}"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
          draggable="false"
        />
      {%- endif %}
    </div>

    <div class="work-card__details">
      <div class="work-card__text">
        <p class="work-card__number" aria-hidden="true">{{ "0" + index }}</p>
        <h3 class="work-card__title">{{ project.card.title }}</h3>
        <p class="work-card__body">{{ project.card.body }}</p>
      </div>

      {%- if project.url %}
        {{ button(
          label="Read more",
          href=project.url,
          iconName="arrow-right",
          variant="solid",
          aria="Read more about " + project.title
        ) }}
      {%- endif %}
    </div>
  </article>
{% endmacro %}
